# Dependencies
node_modules/
# Lockfiles ARE committed (removed from this list on 2026-09-26).
# package-lock.json was gitignored, so it was absent from every CI checkout
# and `npm ci` could never run - setup-node with `cache: npm` fails outright
# with "Dependencies lock file is not found". Committing the lock is what
# makes installs reproducible for everyone but the developer.
# yarn.lock / pnpm-lock.yaml / bun.lockb stay ignored: this project uses npm,
# and committing several lockfiles at once is how dependency drift starts.
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
bun.lockb

